      OPIcPhrase(english: "I cook at home most evenings, and over time it's become one of my most fulfilling daily rituals. I spend time each weekend planning meals and sourcing good ingredients, which makes the actual cooking feel intentional rather than rushed. Sharing what I've made with someone I care about is one of my most consistent sources of genuine happiness.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "There's a small family-run restaurant in my neighborhood that I've been going to for nearly three years. The menu is simple and hasn't changed much, but every dish is made with obvious care and pride. It's the kind of place that makes you feel welcomed rather than served, and I keep coming back because of that.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've become increasingly interested in the origins and production methods of the food I eat. Knowing that something was grown locally, raised humanely, or produced by artisans changes how I experience it. I shop at farmers' markets when I can, and the quality and flavor genuinely reflect that difference.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Breakfast is a meal I take seriously, because I've learned how directly it shapes my energy and concentration throughout the morning. I make time for a proper breakfast even on busy weekday mornings — something with protein, something fresh, and a good cup of coffee. The days I skip it, I notice the difference immediately.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Dining with family or friends is something I prioritize regardless of how busy life gets. There's a quality to connection that happens around a shared meal that doesn't happen in quite the same way anywhere else. Some of my most important conversations and warmest memories have happened over food.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I took a cooking class in Italian cuisine several months ago, and it completely changed how I cook at home. Learning proper technique from a skilled instructor gave me tools I now use every week. It reminded me that there's always more to learn in the kitchen, no matter how long you've been cooking.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I'm genuinely adventurous when it comes to food, and I've almost never regretted trying something unfamiliar. Some dishes I was most hesitant about have turned out to be among my absolute favorites. I think approaching food with openness is a kind of practice for approaching the world the same way.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I appreciate restaurants that treat ingredients with respect and let quality speak for itself. The best meals I've had aren't necessarily the most elaborate — they're the ones where every element on the plate tastes like what it actually is. That honesty in cooking is something I find deeply satisfying.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Street food holds a special place in my food-loving heart, especially when I'm traveling. Some of the most memorable and delicious things I've ever eaten have come from a cart or a street stall. There's a directness and energy to street food that formal restaurants often can't replicate.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've been exploring more plant-based cooking at home over the past year, partly for health reasons and partly out of curiosity. It's pushed me to discover ingredients and flavor combinations I never would have tried otherwise. My cooking has become more diverse and more creative as a result.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The atmosphere and service of a restaurant matter enormously to me — sometimes more than the food itself. A place where the staff are genuinely warm, the space is comfortable, and the pace feels unhurried turns a good meal into a memorable experience. I'd rather eat simple food in a beautiful setting than elaborate food in a cold one.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've started cooking dishes from different countries as a way of exploring cultures I'm curious about. Looking up traditional recipes, sourcing the right ingredients, and learning the techniques feels like a small kind of travel. And the result is always a meal with a story behind it.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "A long, leisurely Sunday lunch has become one of my most cherished weekly rituals. I take my time preparing something more elaborate than a weekday meal and invite friends or family to share it. That unhurried eating and conversation is one of the highlights of my week.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I believe that learning to cook well is one of the most valuable life skills a person can develop. It gives you control over what you eat, saves money, and creates a foundation for hospitality and generosity. Every time I feed someone a good meal, I feel a deep and uncomplicated kind of satisfaction.", korean: "", topic: '음식·식당'),
    ],

    '건강·운동': [
      OPIcPhrase(english: "My approach to health has evolved from something reactive — exercising when I felt guilty — to something genuinely proactive. I now see fitness, nutrition, sleep, and mental health as interconnected pillars that support everything else I do. When all four are in balance, I function at a level that's noticeably different from when any one is neglected.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I started strength training about two years ago after years of only doing cardio, and the change has been remarkable. Beyond the physical transformation, the discipline of showing up consistently and tracking progress has shaped my mindset. I've brought that same structured, goal-oriented approach into my professional and personal life.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Sleep is the health habit I've become most protective of over the past few years. I've experimented with my schedule and discovered that seven and a half hours is the amount where I feel genuinely sharp and energized. Everything else — my workouts, my work, my relationships — functions better when I'm truly well rested.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I went through a period of serious burnout a few years ago, and it fundamentally changed how I think about mental health. I realized that I had been treating stress like a badge of honor rather than a warning sign. Now I take active steps to manage my stress level — through exercise, time in nature, and regular reflection.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Nutrition has become increasingly important to me as I've learned how directly it affects my mood and energy. I now cook most of my meals from scratch, prioritizing whole foods and minimizing processed ingredients. The connection between what I eat and how I feel is so direct that I can't imagine going back to my previous habits.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Running has been part of my life for three years, and I've gone from barely finishing a 5K to completing my first half marathon. The training process taught me as much about mental resilience as it did about physical fitness. I now know that what feels impossible at the start of a training plan becomes achievable through consistent, patient effort.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I practice yoga three times a week, and it has become one of the most non-negotiable parts of my routine. The combination of physical challenge, breathwork, and mindfulness is unlike anything else I've found. I leave every session feeling longer, calmer, and more in my own body than when I arrived.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I injured my ankle badly during a trail run about a year ago and had to stop all exercise for six weeks. It was one of the most frustrating experiences of my life, but it also taught me to listen to my body and respect its limits. I came back stronger, but more importantly, I came back smarter about training and recovery.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I use a health tracking app that logs my workouts, sleep, and nutrition, and reviewing that data has been genuinely eye-opening. I've spotted patterns I never would have noticed otherwise — like how closely my sleep quality correlates with my stress levels. That visibility has made me a much more informed and intentional steward of my own health.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I try to integrate movement into my day in ways that don't require a gym or structured workout. I walk wherever possible, take stairs instead of elevators, and do stretching during breaks at my desk. Those small habits add up significantly over the course of a day and week.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Hydration is the health habit I've been most surprised by in terms of impact. I started tracking my water intake six months ago and quickly realized I had been chronically under-hydrated. Drinking adequate water daily has improved my skin, reduced headaches, and noticeably sharpened my concentration.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've come to view exercise less as a tool for changing my body and more as a form of mental maintenance. On the days I work out, I'm calmer, more focused, and more patient with the people around me. That shift in motivation — from aesthetic to functional — has made staying consistent far easier.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I started doing outdoor trail runs on weekends after years of running exclusively on a treadmill. The difference is profound — the varied terrain, fresh air, and natural scenery make the same distance feel like a completely different activity. I now look forward to Saturday trail runs in a way I never felt about the gym.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "A comprehensive health check-up I had recently gave me a clear picture of where I stand physically. Most results were good, but a few areas prompted me to make targeted changes to my diet and exercise habits. I found the whole process clarifying and motivating rather than anxiety-inducing.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "My long-term relationship with exercise has taught me that consistency matters far more than intensity. A moderate workout done four times a week for years produces results that no crash fitness program ever could. I try to remember that whenever I'm tempted to look for shortcuts.", korean: "", topic: '건강·운동'),
    ],

    '날씨·계절': [
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Spring is my favorite season, and I look forward to it all through the grey months of winter. When the first warm days arrive and the cherry blossoms come out, the whole city seems to exhale with relief. I spend as much time outdoors as possible during those brief, perfect weeks before the heat sets in.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Autumn has a particular quality of light that I find deeply beautiful and a little melancholy at the same time. The cooling air, the changing leaves, and the smell of the season all feel like a gentle reminder that change is natural and worthwhile. I find myself most creative and reflective during autumn, which makes it my most productive season by far.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Rainy days have a special quality that I genuinely love, especially when I'm at home. There's a particular kind of coziness to being indoors with a book or a slow meal while rain falls steadily outside. Those days feel like permission to slow down, and I've come to cherish them.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The summers here are intensely hot and humid in a way that demands real adaptation. I've adjusted my schedule to avoid being outside during the hottest hours, doing my outdoor activities early in the morning or after sunset. I've also discovered that summer has its own beauty — the long evenings, the cicadas, the thunderstorms.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The first snowfall of the year is something I never quite get used to, no matter how many times I've experienced it. The way it silences the city, transforms the familiar landscape, and makes everything look clean and new is genuinely magical for a few hours. I always try to get outside during that first snowfall before the slush and reality set in.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've become much more attentive to seasonal changes since starting a balcony garden. Watching plants respond to temperature shifts, daylight changes, and rainfall has made me notice things about the seasons I completely overlooked before. It's given me a kind of intimacy with the natural world that I hadn't expected.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Weather has a more significant effect on my mood than I used to acknowledge. Prolonged grey, cold weather genuinely drags on my energy and outlook, while bright sunny days lift me immediately. Recognizing this has helped me take proactive steps — like using a light therapy lamp in winter — to manage that effect.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Cold weather triggers a deep instinct in me to cook hearty, warming foods. Soups, braises, and baked dishes become my weekly staples from October through March. There's something primally satisfying about a hot meal on a cold day that lighter summer cooking just doesn't provide.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've found that the transitional seasons — spring and autumn — are when I feel most alive and engaged with the world. The moderate temperatures invite outdoor activity, the changing scenery provides constant visual interest, and there's an energy of beginning or ending that I find stimulating. I try to make the most of these fleeting windows every year.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Typhoon season is genuinely dramatic here, and I've developed a healthy respect for it. I prepare carefully — stocking supplies, checking forecasts, and making sure everything on my balcony is secured. But there's also something awe-inspiring about watching nature operate at that scale, safely from indoors.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've started planning seasonal activities deliberately, rather than letting each season slip by without marking it. In spring I go to see cherry blossoms; in summer I swim; in autumn I hike for the foliage; in winter I ski once if I can. That structure gives me something to anticipate in every season and ensures I engage with the year rather than just endure it.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Winter mornings are the greatest test of my discipline throughout the year. Leaving a warm bed and a warm apartment to face cold, dark streets takes real motivation. But I've found that people who push through that resistance and get moving early in winter feel a particular pride and clarity that easier seasons don't produce.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The yellow and red foliage of late October is one of the year's most reliable pleasures. I plan at least one hiking trip to the mountains when the colors are at their peak, and it's consistently one of the highlights of my year. There's a beauty to that season that feels almost impossibly vivid.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I track the weather forecast carefully because it shapes so many of my daily decisions. What I wear, what I cook, whether I walk or take public transport, what outdoor plans I make — all of it responds to the weather. I've found that working with the climate rather than against it makes daily life much more pleasant.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Living through distinct four seasons is something I deeply appreciate, even when individual seasons are uncomfortable. Each one brings its own rhythms, foods, activities, and emotional textures. I think the contrast is what makes each season feel special — you truly appreciate warmth only after months of cold.", korean: "", topic: '날씨·계절'),
    ],

    '집·동네': [
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've lived in my current apartment for three years, and I've invested real time and care in making it feel like home. I've filled it with plants, books, and things that have personal meaning, and the result is a space that genuinely reflects who I am. I feel a deep sense of peace and comfort the moment I walk through the door.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "My neighborhood has become as important to my daily life as my apartment itself. I know the vendors at the Saturday market, I have a regular table at my favorite café, and I feel a genuine sense of belonging walking these streets. That rootedness in a particular place is something I've come to value enormously.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I made the deliberate choice to live in a smaller apartment in a central, walkable neighborhood rather than a larger place further out. The trade-off has been completely worth it — I walk everywhere, spend less on transport, and feel deeply connected to city life. Living small has also forced a kind of curation and intentionality about what I own that I find satisfying.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Living close to a large park has been one of the great gifts of my current address. I run there in the mornings, walk there in the evenings, and sit there on weekends when I need to think. Access to green space in the middle of a city is something I would find very difficult to give up.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I share my apartment with a roommate, which has turned out to be a much richer experience than I expected. We come from different backgrounds and have different habits, and navigating that has taught me a great deal about communication and compromise. We've also become genuine friends, which is something I didn't anticipate when we first moved in together.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I recently spent several weeks renovating and redecorating my living room, and the transformation has been remarkable. Beyond the aesthetic improvement, the process taught me practical skills I'm proud of and gave me a real sense of ownership over my space. I now feel much more motivated to keep the apartment beautiful and well-maintained.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The community aspect of my neighborhood is something I didn't fully appreciate when I first moved here. Over time I've gotten to know local business owners, neighbors who've lived here for decades, and regular faces at the park. That web of familiar, friendly connections makes the neighborhood feel like a village inside the city.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "Working from home several days a week has completely changed my relationship with my apartment. It's no longer just a place to sleep and eat — it's the environment where I think, create, and solve problems. That shift has motivated me to invest seriously in making it functional, comfortable, and conducive to focus.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I moved to this neighborhood for practical reasons — good transport links and proximity to work. But I've stayed because I genuinely love the character of the area: the mix of old and new, the local food scene, the people. It's one of those places that surprises you by becoming more interesting the longer you spend in it.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've become much more intentional about how I use the space in my apartment since I started working from home. I've created distinct zones for work, relaxation, and creative activity, and that separation has helped me maintain boundaries between different parts of my day. Living and working in the same space requires real design thinking to make both work well.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The Saturday market near my apartment has become a weekly ritual I genuinely look forward to. I pick up seasonal produce, browse the handmade goods, and usually run into neighbors I know. It's a simple thing, but it does more for my sense of community than almost anything else in my week.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I gave up my car when I moved to this neighborhood and haven't missed it once. The subway access is excellent, everything I need daily is walkable, and cycling takes care of everything in between. The money I've saved has been significant, and I feel better about my environmental footprint.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "I've been thinking about what my ideal long-term living situation looks like, and it's not dramatically different from what I have now. I'd like slightly more space, perhaps a proper second room, but I want to stay in this neighborhood. The relationships and routines I've built here feel genuinely irreplaceable.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "My apartment has become a place I actively enjoy spending time, which wasn't always the case. I've made it comfortable enough to work, creative enough to inspire me, and cozy enough that I never feel restless at home. Home should feel like a sanctuary, and I feel fortunate that mine finally does.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
      OPIcPhrase(english: "The urban environment I live in offers something I've come to deeply value: constant low-level stimulation and access to variety. On any given evening I can choose from dozens of restaurants, venues, and experiences within walking distance. That richness of options is something rural or suburban life couldn't offer, and it keeps me genuinely engaged with where I live.", korean: "", topic: '집·동네'),
    ],

  };
